<title>DENMARK: Danish July current account 0.0 bln DKK.</title>
<headline>Danish July current account 0.0 bln DKK.</headline>
<dateline>COPENHAGEN 1996-10-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>Denmark's current account stood at 0.0 billion crowns in July, from a revised 1.3 billion crown surplus in June, the national statistics office said on Friday.  </p>
<p>DANISH CURRENT ACCOUNT (billions of crowns)</p>
<p>Figures for the past three, six and 12 month periods:</p>
<p>			 Three-month Six-month Twelve-month</p>
<p>Current account	 +2.9	 +7.3	  +9.6</p>
<p>Goods		    +11.2	+21.9	 +40.6</p>
<p>Services		  +2.7	 +3.7	  +5.2</p>
<p>Interest, other	-11.0	-18.4	 -36.2</p>
<p>NOTE - Figures are subject to rounding. Market analysts polled by Reuters had predicted an average July current account surplus of 0.4 billion crowns.</p>
<p>--Chris Follett, Copenhagen newsroom +45-33-969650</p>
</text>
